<title>UK: SOCCER-SCOTTISH CLUB PLANS STOCK MARKET FLOAT.</title>
<headline>SOCCER-SCOTTISH CLUB PLANS STOCK MARKET FLOAT.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Scottish soccer club Hearts of Midlothian on Sunday announced plans for a listing on the London Stock Exchange by early May.</p>
<p>The premier league club aims to raise about five to million pounds ($8.0 to $9.6 million) by placing new shares with institutional investors.</p>
<p>The proceeds will be used to build a new, 3,500 seater stadium stand and reduce borrowings.</p>
<p>Hearts said it does not intend to spend the money on new players.</p>
<p>The club is being advised by stockbroker Williams de Broe.</p>
